// EXPECT-DIAG: E040
// EXPECT-DIAG: E108
// EXPECT-DIAG: Expected a parameter name in the parameter list
// Regression test for issue #245: SkipToNextTopLevelBoundary()'s brace-depth
// counter used to permanently mis-track when a failed top-level construct
// opened a '(' it never got to close (the parse error fires before any
// matching ')' is ever seen) -- every declaration after the broken one was
// silently swallowed as "still skipping" instead of being recovered and
// reported on its own.
//
// This file must still fail to compile (the runner only checks pass/fail),
// but confirmed via `turf --resolve` directly: before the fix, only the
// line-1 parse error was ever reported; after the fix, the line-4
// "undefined reference" error below is ALSO reported, proving `ok()`'s body
// (and `main()`) were actually recovered and parsed/resolved instead of
// being swallowed by the permanently-offset brace-depth counter.
fn broken(: int {
    }

    fn ok(): int {
        return undefinedVariableXyz;
    }

    fn main(): int {
        return ok();
    }
